A||||30||ChadMan||Sentra or Saturn?||||5||
Z||000000||ChadMan||05-18-2001||08:58 AM||||My parents need a new car and have very little money, so my wife and I are selling them her '95 Saturn SL1 and buying a new car.  We have narrowed the search down to the Sentra GXE and the Saturn SL2.<P>Both cars are loaded option-wise and our monthly payment would be about the same (Saturn is more expensive but is offering 0.9 financing).  Both cars make about 125 hp and get 25/35 mpg.  I have no doubt either car will go 200k miles if we maintain it well, and we will.<P>The Sentra seems to be a better engineered car and rides/drives a little nicer, but the Saturn will never rust, plus there's that intangible "Fiero's cousin" appeal.<P>Which would you choose?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Black88GT||05-18-2001||09:05 AM||||<B>GET THE SENTRA!!</B><P>Chadman, my mom just bought a fully loaded Sentra SE.  This car is sweeeeet.  It's got the SE performance package including 16" wheels, power sunroof, spoiler, strut tower brace, front/rear sway bars, 4 wheel discs, CD player, lumbar seat, white faced gauges, and fog lights.  Oh the SE's have the 150 hp 2.0 DOHC (same engine in infinity G20s).  I love this car!  It looks like a mini-Maxima.  She was looking at Saturns too but you can't get the same reliability in a Saturn as in a Nissan.  I think overall she paid 16,500 and they threw in an extended warranty and floor mats (can't forget the floor mats).  Only thing is my mom got the auto tranny because she doesn't know how to drive a 5 speed, I bet this car would be even more fun with the 5 speed.<P>Oh yeah forgot to add.  My friend has had a late 80s Sentra in their family since it was new.  Car has about 310k miles still going strong.  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 05-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||05-18-2001||09:30 AM||||Get the Nissan... they live forever. <P>I like the Saturns, but given a choice between the two, I feel certain you will get more longevity from the Nissan. (This is coming from a guy whose family (two parents, five kids, two grandkids) has owned over 20 Nissan/Datsuns...)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-18-2001||10:28 AM||||I would get the Saturn. You can't beat their customer service and the reliability is excellent. I had a 94 Saturn and in 6 years it was to the dealer only once for a repair.<BR>A relative has a 96 Sentra which has been to the dealer many times. (Bad injector, door seals falling off, exhaust heat shield falling off, bad alternator, just to name a few.) I sold the Saturn because we needed a bigger car, I was sorry to see it go.<BR>I'm going to miss the free car washes in winter. (Saturn will run the car thru the car wash anytime you want, for free!)<BR>Finally, from a saftey point, A Saturn is much Safer than the Sentra in in accident. (4-stars vs. 5 stars)<BR>This is just my opinion. <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||05-18-2001||10:42 AM||||One of my favorite sites for car opinions is <A HREF="http://www.carreview.com" TARGET=_blank>www.carreview.com</A>   <P>To save you time here are the links for the Sentra and the Saturn SL series.  (sentra got a full point higher in overall feedback rating)<P> <A HREF="http://www.carreview.com/reviews/midsize_compacts/product_284.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://www.carreview.com/reviews/midsize_compacts/product_284.shtml</A>  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.carreview.com/reviews/midsize_compacts/product_297.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://www.carreview.com/reviews/midsize_compacts/product_297.shtml</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||05-18-2001||11:13 AM||||Black88GT, That's an interesting site! You can tell by the reviews who actually rated the car and who's an idiot.  From what I read in the reviews, It seems the cars are about equal. Some had "problem cars" some didn't. The funniest was the moron with the 94 sentra. He states he hasn't done any engine work and he doesn't even know what engine is in it! But he states he has 450hp, can go 0-60 in 4.5 seconds, does 80mph lane changes, and hasn't found a car that could beat his! The 95 Saturn SL1 guy who says the 5-spd trans doesn't hold up to weekly street racing isn't too bright either. 61,000 miles and he's replaced the trans 4 times. HMM maybe he shouldn't beat the hell out of the car.<BR>Anyhow, I've bookmarked the site.<BR>Thanks.||||reg||10
Z||000006||Black88GT||05-18-2001||11:30 AM||||Oreif, I love that site!  I go there a lot to check out new car reviews.  Your right about the idiots too.  One guy said about the Sentra "Besides the strength of the car,I don't think it's a good racing car for the road,come on people,look at toyota corrola for crying out loud" (lmao) so he rated it low.  Another guy said it didn't have as much pass. space as a Camry (well - DUH) so he gave it all 1's.  I mean, this site has to be taken with a grain of salt.  You can't use it as a bible for cars.  But it is a decent reference when buying new cars.  I mean cars that have over a 4 rating on that site I would consider good.  If you really want to laugh your butt off, check out the reviews for the Kia's and Daewoo's.  Oh man they are hillarious...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Butter||05-18-2001||11:55 AM||||Go with as much American Iron as you can.  I try to support u s.||||reg||14
Z||000008||p4n1c||05-18-2001||12:00 PM||||Pretty good site.  I posted a review on my car.  People were whining about it, but if they actually took care of the car and didn't beat the hell out of it.  They wouldn't have problems.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000009||DRH||05-18-2001||02:37 PM||||My daughter just got a new Saturn SL2 and loves it. She got the .9 for 5 years deal. Can't beat that... kinda like "5 years same as cash".<P>If I were in the market for that kind of car I believe that's what I'd get. They seem well engineered and well built. Plus you'd help support US manufacturing with the new concept of union-management cooperation...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fformula88||05-18-2001||08:20 PM||||I'd go Saturn over the. First is the plastic side panels!  If you keep the car 200K miles, you won't want to drive the second 100K without any rear fenders.  Also, it won't look like it was a backstop for a little league from parking lot dents a month after you take it home!<P>I've also heard hardly any criticisms of Saturns.  Everybody I know who owns one absolutely loves it!  Mechanically they seem to be very reliable.<P>It doesn't sound like you can wait to buy, but Saturn will be intorducing a completely redesigned S series within a year or two.  This car is moving to an all new platform, so I would assume it will catch them up in engineering with the competition!  I'm also hoping they add a few more ponies under the hood (like putting the L series V6 into the SC2!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000011||JJ-85-2M6||05-18-2001||08:45 PM||||Get the Saturn if you are looking for a long term vehicle.  I've had my Sc2 for 8 years (reliable and great dealer service).  It also looks great due to the plastic body panels.  Overall, the Nissan is probably a bit more reliable, but I hate how quickly some Japanese cars get "pock marked" with parking lot dents. ||||reg||10
Z||000012||frontal lobe||05-18-2001||11:50 PM||||I feel so unpatriotic, but I'd go with the Sentra.  Smoother engine, more back seat room (an issue?).  But it's a close call and you couldn't make a bad choice in this case.||||reg||1
Z||000013||beer_stud_21||05-19-2001||05:07 AM||||just went to that car review site, had to read some daiwoo reviews.. Just had to share this one with you folks.  To funny...<P>Weaknesses: Dints TOOO easy, squeeky brakes (but they work good), not a good looking car with that long bonnet and a bonnet grill that looks like Krusty the Clown high on pot!<BR> <BR>Compared To: Drove a Honda Civic, the only thing better is the body and the brakes don't squeak. <P>Review Summary: Overall it's a nice car. If I changed those big daft black bumpers and put some custom kit on, it'd be VERY nice.  <P>Guy is obviously from europe somewhere, but the whole krusty the clown on pot thing.. ROTFLOL!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Marlin<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||beer_stud_21||05-19-2001||05:19 AM||||you guys gotta read this... <BR> <A HREF="http://www.carreview.com/reviews/midsize_compacts/product_265.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://www.carreview.com/reviews/midsize_compacts/product_265.shtml</A> <P>just to funny..<P>-Marlin (again)||||reg||1
Z||000015||Black88GT||05-19-2001||06:24 PM||||Haha listen to this on the Daewoo Lanos:<P>" Well, first, the car (if that's called a car) falls apart as you look at it. Riding it only makes it worse. It was the worst thing I ever bought. The toolkit should have come with it. It's not believable how many problems I had with this car: First, for no reason, the windshield came off when I was going about 60 mph. Daewoo fixed it and said it was "a manufacturer default". Then, the motor blew on me. After having that fixed, the grill-like thing in front of the car flew on the highroad and one of my back doors couldn't open nor close anymore. Oh, and the brakes only seemed to work on the left side of the car, the other side kidda gave a burnt metal smell. It's a good thing I didn't pay for the repair and I was extremely happy when I sold it at the scrap yard for 300$. WILL NEVER BUY FROM DAEWOO AGAIN. Heck, all Daewoo's good for is for TVs. And are they good at that? "||||reg||1
Z||000016||Nikotek||05-20-2001||12:11 AM||||It's a no-brainer,the Nissan is twice the car Saturn is in every aspect easily!I own a twin turbo Z and my wife has a 2000 Maxima. The Sentra is in effect a baby Maxima-the materials,quality and performance are outstanding.My brother-in-law has a Saturn which sort of reminds me of my first car a mid 80's Toyota Tercel alot...cheaply made.No offense meant to any Saturn owners,they have come a long way in a short time.Good-Luck!<P>------------------<BR>87' GT (355 Spyder)<BR>88' Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000017||pHoOl||05-20-2001||09:08 AM||||a few things for me to add...<P>first off, i would check into things like prices for servicing.  everything that i have seen shows imports being way more to fix than american.  I owned a 92SL1 and i missed it like crazy when i got rid of it.  And the dent proof sides were great.  Didn't realize how much cars get hit in highschool parking lots until i had my pickup truck.  Oh, btw, yes, those doors are quite dent resistant.  Took a baseball bat to it many times without a scratch.  (Dad worked for Saturn, he was confident in their engineering and had to show it to anyone who came over)<P>just my $.02<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||ChadMan||05-21-2001||08:39 AM||||We bought the Saturn -- a loaded SL2, 60 months at 0.9%.  It's a really nice cranberry red that's a little darker than my Fiero.<P>Honestly, I liked the Sentra a little better - it drove a little nicer and seemed slightly better built.  But my wife liked the Saturn, and here in the road salt capitol of the world, those plastic panels are a HUGE advantage (I know you Fieroholics know what I'm talking about).  And 0.9 financing for 5 years is unbeatable.  I'm glad Angie likes it because she will be driving it for a LONG time.<P>Thanks for all the advice.||||reg||14
Z||000019||JJ-85-2M6||05-21-2001||07:59 PM||||Congratulations! Those plastic panels have a great clearcoat too.  Looks wet!<P>J||||reg||10
Z||000020||frontal lobe||05-22-2001||01:31 AM||||Nice move, Chadman.  Hey, SHE is the one driving it mainly, so let her have her way on that one.  Nice financing.  If you do keep that car a long time, which you will be able to, you will make out very well financially on it.<P>Stick or auto?||||reg||1
Z||000021||ChadMan||05-22-2001||09:28 AM||||Thanks!  We got the auto...my wife doesn't like driving a stick shift.  Of course, that means I don't have to share my Fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000022||Ken Wittlief||05-22-2001||01:41 PM||||you done good! Look at the retail values of sentras after 4 or 5 years compaired to saturns - sentras do not hold their value.<P> I have a 94SL2 Homecoming Special, a 2000 SL 5 speed that get 45mpg at 75mph with the AC on, and we just got a 2001 L200 for the wife.<P>  in last years crash test the saturn was the only car the survived a 5mph crash into a brick wall with ZERO! damage - some other cars had thousands of $$$ damage - and on the Volvo the AIR BAGS WENT OFF - $6000 repair bill at 5mph!<P>  I talked to a guy who bought one of those hybrid electics, cant remeber which one, paid $18,000 for it and he gets 60mpg. When I told him I get 45mpg in my 4 passenger SL, with the AC on, and I only paid $12,000 for it, his jaw dropped. gas is only 5 to 7% the expense of owning a car - he paid 50% more for a car that gets 33% better mileage<P> or in other words, he will save about $1100 in the cost of fuel over my car after driving 100,000 miles, and he paid $6,000 more for the priviledge.<P> saturns are great, they are also our best hope of a GM company making another 2 seater commuter car. I would love to see a new saturn model, 2 passenger, rear engine, plastic body panels, space frame, stainless steel exhaust, hydralic clutch <BR> <BR>  hey wait, that sounds familiar!||||reg||1
Z||000023||Black88GT||05-22-2001||03:51 PM||||I decided to take Ken up on his offer and "Look at the retail values of sentras after 4 or 5 years compaired to saturns"<P>So thats what I did.  I took a '96 Sentra GXE, standard equipment except for auto tranny.  Then I took a comparable '96 SL1 Saturn, used standard options except for auto tranny, and looked them up on <A HREF="http://www.kbb.com." TARGET=_blank>www.kbb.com.</A>   The site gives you what the mileage "should" be for a '96, 68k miles, so I used that for both.  Same zip code also.<P>Retail for the Sentra - $8,280<BR>Retail for the Saturn - $7,135 <P> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Ken Wittlief||05-22-2001||04:20 PM||||ok and how much did those two cars sell for originally?||||reg||1
Z||000025||Ken Wittlief||05-22-2001||04:21 PM||||the other thing to keep in mind, how much the blue book value is, and how much people are actually selling them for, can be way different.||||reg||1
Z||000026||Ken Wittlief||05-22-2001||04:31 PM||||also, the book value is used for cars that are less then 4 or 5 years old to establish insurance payoff values when a car is totalled - look at cars in the paper or in the swap sheet publications that are more like 6 or 7 years old. ||||reg||1
Z||000027||DRH||05-22-2001||05:00 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.edmunds.com" TARGET=_blank>www.edmunds.com</A>  seems to have prices more in line with what cars are actually selling for in the real world. Plus you can see trade-in, individual and dealer prices side by side. <P>KBB seems to be more of a dealer's tool to use with customers... The retail values always seem high and the trade in values always seem low.<P>Chadman, sounds like exactly the car my daughter just bought. ||||reg||1
Z||000028||Oreif||05-22-2001||06:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>I decided to take Ken up on his offer and "Look at the retail values of sentras after 4 or 5 years compaired to saturns"<P>So thats what I did.  I took a '96 Sentra GXE, standard equipment except for auto tranny.  Then I took a comparable '96 SL1 Saturn, used standard options except for auto tranny, and looked them up on <A HREF="http://www.kbb.com." TARGET=_blank>www.kbb.com.</A>   The site gives you what the mileage "should" be for a '96, 68k miles, so I used that for both.  Same zip code also.<P>Retail for the Sentra - $8,280<BR>Retail for the Saturn - $7,135 <P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Saturn SL2 is more like the GXE The SL1 is like the XE and the SL is like the base Sentra. If you go by this, the Saturn is higher value than the Sentra. You need to compare the cars with the same trim level.<BR>KBB doesn't list the "standard" and "optional" items correctly for both cars.<P> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Black88GT||05-22-2001||09:19 PM||||Ahhh I knew I would get this.<P>OK, my purpose was not to find what these cars would sell for or whatever.  My purpose was to look up the "retail" value, the value you would find at a dealer, at an unbiased website. <P>The Saturn SL2 is the TOP OF THE LINE Saturn.  The Sentra SE is the top of the line Sentra.  The SL1 is one step below the top of the line, the GXE is one step below the top of the line.  <P>Whether they give the options right or not is irrelevent.  You could load up the Saturn and it still wouldn't add 1,000 dollars to the value.  <P>My point wasn't to show the Sentra is necessarily better but it does hold its value (like any other japanese car), contrary to what was posted.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000030||fierogt88||05-23-2001||02:35 PM||||I'd say go with the saturn.<P>You have narrowed it down well.  Both cars are great family vehicles, and either choice will serve you well.  A few suggestions...  Check out the safety ratings.  Saturn wins that one.  Walk up to any saturn and pound on the door panels. hard. harder.  yep. no dents. no cracked paint.  I test out my doors all the time and it still looks new.  and its american.  I'm sure nissan has its good points too, but the saturn "wins" in all the right places for me.  and there are really only two car companies I trust to stand behind their products.... nissan and saturn.  both of them have performance mods available too.  (nothing like our fiero, but still... )<P>if anything puts the saturn over the top (for me) it's the fact that its safer and the fact that its american.  those were the important ones for me.<P>oh and i think the sentra is ugly and the saturn is beautiful, but you know what they say about the beholder....||||reg||1
